<title>UK: UK'S CHARLES SYDNEY NAMES NEW CEO.</title>
<headline>UK'S CHARLES SYDNEY NAMES NEW CEO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>British car and commercial vehicle dealer and rental operator Charles Sidney Plc said on Tuesday Raymond Edwards had been appointed chief executive of the company, replacing John Ross.</p>
<p>Ross left the company on Monday but the company did not say why.</p>
<p>Edwards was the non-executive chairman of the company and has been replaced in that post by Jack Mather, a non-executive director.</p>
